# =============================================================================
# TRACE-Kin v3 PER-FOLDER + ChemBERT — top-10 RF-gap cells
# =============================================================================
# Submit with:
#     bsub < training/run_v3_perfolder_s1.lsf
#
# Per-folder evaluation: each (dataset × kinetic × split) cell gets its own
# v3 model trained ONLY on that folder's train.parquet, tested on that
# folder's test.parquet. NO cross-dataset pooling — avoids the leakage
# concern that pool-train rows could contaminate primary-test keys.
#
# v3 FP-MLP head input is mean-ESM (1280) ⊕ ChemBERT (768), loaded from
# the per-row `metabolite_features` column of train/val/test.parquet —
# apples-to-apples vs the historical ChemBERT-fed RF baseline.
#
# Cells: the 10 (out of 27) where the historical PSICHIC-vs-RF gap is
# largest, derived from data/benchmark/kinetic_regress_benchmark_clean.csv.
# These are the cells the ChemBERT cutover is most likely to move. The
# embedding per cell is the one with the LOWEST RF baseline RMSE in the
# benchmark (= the hardest fair test for v3). All 5 kinetics, all 3 splits,
# and all 4 source datasets are represented.
#
# Ordered by descending RF-gap (PSICHIC RMSE − RF RMSE):
#   1. EITLEM   kcat_km cold_drug    ESMv1       gap +0.135
#   2. catpred  kcat    random       ESMv1       gap +0.130
#   3. inhouse  Kd      random       ESMv1       gap +0.115
#   4. EITLEM   kcat_km random       ESM2        gap +0.098
#   5. EITLEM   kcat    cold_drug    ESM2        gap +0.093
#   6. MPEK     kcat    cold_protein ProteinCLIP gap +0.092
#   7. EITLEM   km      cold_protein ProteinCLIP gap +0.090
#   8. catpred  ki      cold_protein ProteinCLIP gap +0.085
#   9. EITLEM   kcat_km cold_protein ProteinCLIP gap +0.080
#  10. EITLEM   kcat    cold_protein ProteinCLIP gap +0.073
#
# Outputs land under TRACE_Kin_Results_v3_chembert/<dataset>/<task_name>/
# so they don't collide with the existing TRACE_Kin_Results_v3*/ trees.

(... more ...)
